 "harnessFindings": [
  "The lesson page lists the lesson's messages from EVERY session (history is lesson-scoped; ending a session does not hide it - verified with three sessions, two ended, page still held all three replies), so a retry adds another card. The harness framed document.querySelector(...) = the FIRST card, so 18 retries on normal-force/equilibrium kept measuring the first, short reply (\"normal arrow drawn in the page = false\" every time). Fixed in scripts/qa/physicsProductionBrowserAudit.ts: the LAST card is framed. Retry path verified: equilibrium replies of 3,7,3,9 lines measured a card that draws the normal arrow (the first, 3-line card cannot); normal-force replies 4,6,4,3 measured the last 3-line card and correctly drew no normal arrow. Run Z1 (6-line reply, first attempt) reached all five steps.",
  "A card shows as many steps as the page's own narration has segments; a 3-sentence reply leaves steps 4-5 unseen. That is the lesson card's design (visualStepForSegment), not a diagram defect; a pass is only claimed for a step that was seen."
 ],
 "contrastObservation": "CT-01 FAIL on \"Applied\" (3.99:1 dark / 3.11:1 light) and \"Friction\" (3.61:1 dark / 3.43:1 light) - exactly the authored, un-lifted colours - in 4 of about 40 harness measurements for this closure, each on a page holding several cards (retries), measured on an OLDER card (the harness framed the first card). ROOT CAUSE (reproduced in production, offscreen probe): useFigureLegibility finds the text backdrop with document.elementsFromPoint, which only hits what is inside the viewport; a card mounted outside the viewport (an older figure above the fold of a restored lesson) gets no contrast lift and nothing re-runs the pass when it is scrolled into view (three cards on a 390x844 page: the in-view card lifted, the two older ones all 'plain', still plain 6 s after scrolling the first into view). Pre-existing, in shared code used by every subject's 2D figures; NOT fixed in this closure - owner decision (proposed fix: re-run the pass when the figure enters the viewport, an IntersectionObserver in the hook). Every single-card page lifted (run Z1, the Y1 equilibrium run of one attempt, the one-attempt probe, 18 direct probes).",
 "disposableAccounts": "every run ended with \"disposable account deleted = true\"; two accounts orphaned when a worker restart killed runs X1/X2 were found by email pattern, logged into with the generated credentials and deleted through DELETE /api/user/delete-account (deleted=true, relogin blocked)."
